WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.608
Cao Cao led an army said to number eight hundred thousand, sailing grandly down the river, pressing straight toward Jiangdong.

00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:13.478
On the river the warships stretched out in one expanse, their banners fluttering in the wind.

00:00:13.828 --> 00:00:20.956
Sun Quan and Liu Bei decided to ally; though they had only fifty thousand men, they arrayed their forces at Red Cliffs.

00:00:21.306 --> 00:00:29.658
Zhou Yu and Zhuge Liang discussed strategy and agreed: only a fire attack could let the few defeat the many.

00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:38.888
The veteran Huang Gai steered small boats loaded with straw, pretending to surrender as he slowly approached Cao Cao's warships.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:45.934
At the command, the fire ships launched together, and Cao Cao's chained warships were instantly swallowed by a sea of fire.

00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:50.556
The great fire lit up the whole river, and Cao Cao's soldiers scattered in flight in every direction.

00:00:50.906 --> 00:01:01.274
Cao Cao was badly defeated and fled in disarray with only a few men; the Battle of Red Cliffs thus entered the history books.

